Given $3^{x + y} = 81$ and $81^{x - y} = 3$, we can simplify these equations to find the values of $x$ and $y$. 
\begin{align*}
3^{x + y} &= 3^4 \\
x + y &= 4 \\
\end{align*}
\begin{align*}
81^{x - y} &= 3 \\
(3^4)^{x - y} &= 3 \\
3^{4(x - y)} &= 3^1 \\
4(x - y) &= 1 \\
x - y &= \frac{1}{4} \\
\end{align*}
Solving the system of equations:
\begin{align*}
x + y &= 4 \\
x - y &= \frac{1}{4} \\
\end{align*}
Adding both equations, we get $2x = 4\frac{1}{4}$, so $x = 2\frac{1}{8}$. Substituting $x$ in $x + y = 4$, we get $2\frac{1}{8} + y = 4$, so $y = 1\frac{7}{8}$.</think>
